{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg3NBcyHvBXQfQ8WXAUyC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Browser suite: with the parent's `moveBefore` shadowed by a function that throws, a keyed reorder still produces the new order.\n[x] Browser suite: with the parent's `moveBefore` shadowed by `undefined`, a keyed reorder still produces the new order.\n\nBoth morph fixes for ticket 04 are done and committed. The full `npm test` passes (297/297) and lint is clean.\n\n1. **Duplicate keys (1923c85).** In `src/htm.browser.ts`, `_morph` now checks the keys of a region's new items and throws `duplicate key <k>` before it touches the DOM. Two new tests cover a duplicate in the first `mount` and one that arrives in a later update. In both cases the error comes out of the call that triggered the morph. The existing keyed tests still pass, which covers the \"distinct keys still morph\" item.\n2. **Guarded `moveBefore` (5fd6012).** The placement loop only calls `moveBefore` for kept nodes when the parent is connected. The call is inside a try, and if `moveBefore` is missing or throws, it falls back to `insertBefore`. Errors from `insertBefore` itself are not caught. The tests attach the list to the document and replace `moveBefore` on the `ul` with a throwing function in one test and `undefined` in the other. The throwing case failed before the fix. The `undefined` case already passed, because the old code already fell back to `insertBefore` there, so it stays as a regression guard.\n\n**Size limit raised.** The browser templater grew from 4.6 kB to 4.61 kB, 6 B over its limit. Per the spec's rule I raised the limit to 4.65 kB and noted why in a comment in `.size-limit.js`. I tried smaller versions first, but each one was ruled out:\n- A sentinel `throw 0` fails lint (eslint settings are off-limits).\n- Putting both calls in one try would retry an `insertBefore` that had already failed.\n- A one-expression duplicate check came out bigger after compression.\n\nI also added a short note on both behaviours to the browser templater section of AGENTS.md. My working notes are in `.nightralph/notes.md`, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":585,"cache_read_input_tokens":71501,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":585},"output_tokens":716,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"99e9f71e-6829-41e9-95d7-e48b3b5efe16","uuid":"c5c19504-a45a-4a01-8dda-512040b083d9","timestamp":"2026-10-15T04:08:58.709Z","request_id":"req_011Cg3NBciewtzvYp7CwH6Vc"}
